+# Evidence fixture: the review card without an account
+
+An uncommitted harness for photographing the review screen's behaviour on a device with no WaniKani
+token and no network. It exists because the automation's Enter is not the reader's Enter: a
+`KEYCODE_ENTER` key event reaches `ReactEditText.onKeyUp`, which calls `hideSoftKeyboard()` for any
+single-line input, while the keyboard's visible Done key goes through `ReactTextInputManager`'s
+editor-action listener, which dispatches the submit and returns `true` without blurring. Photographing
+the real behaviour needs the *visible* key pressed, and that needs a queue — which needs an account,
+and no real account may be touched again. This fixture removes the account from the picture.
+
+## One harness, two builds
+
+The same `.evidence-fixture/` directory is compiled into both builds of the pair, so a before/after
+still sits inside identical chrome and identical code; only the app code underneath differs.
+
+| | head — `fix/wanikani-review-feedback` | baseline — `origin/dev` `b8a4b40` |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| APK | `gaten-fixture-head-x86_64-debug.apk` | `gaten-fixture-baseline-x86_64-debug.apk` |
+| sha256 | `d0952c7142bd828680da59d3c0e8505cd7c02c3f69ee832e1b054815cace497e` | `faa521aa22085c7281b5907cddee4fdad857923606e9f32803e98d5eec768247` |
+| size | 205,486,508 B | 205,484,468 B |
+| embedded `assets/index.android.bundle` | 2,695,700 B | 2,694,320 B |
+| marker `Fixture subject: synthetic` | 1 | 1 |
+| marker `A reading is answered in kana` (head-only) | 1 | 0 |
+| marker `No recent searches found` (production shell) | 0 | 0 |
+
+Harness sources (identical in both worktrees, so both APKs carry the same harness revision):
+
+| File | sha256 |
+| --- | --- |
+| `index.js` | `46c8f1c364f3d8b4b7613de8369e100209dcfa2330f1936861c877ad0c5ea39e` |
+| `ReviewFixture.tsx` | `cc88295bacf2b70b829aef5f4dfe619f65cbda23f690fcabb90900a8de1252ce` |
+| `tsconfig.json` | `a29eee3c38477ab73b46a44b919a4fcef1bff6b1d84ed38ad8aa33c5174cdab4` |
+
+The baseline build is made in the `origin/dev` worktree at `/tmp/gaten-dev-baseline` (`b8a4b40`,
+unchanged), which carries a byte-identical copy of this directory and its generated dictionary assets.
+
+## What it renders
+
+The **production** `WaniKaniReview` over the **production** review store. Only the session is handed in:
+
+| Real | Synthetic |
+| --- | --- |
+| `src/rn/ui/review/WaniKaniReview.tsx` (the screen) | one `WaniKaniSession` per scene |
+| `src/rn/ui/review/review-store.ts` — `wkEntry`, `wkCheck`, the kana refusal, `meaningMatches`, phases, wrong counts, `wkContinue`, the retry focus effect | the subject: `仮語` (a non-word), subject id `9001`, four accepted meanings, one reading |
+| `buildWaniKaniPromptOrder` (the pair's order, draws pinned) | `onBack` / `onRetrySubmit` (no-ops) |
+| the app's provider tree from `App.js` | the lookup overlay's `GatenLookupSheet` registration |
+
+The subject is two-part like a Vocabulary card, so the screen quizzes a reading, and it carries four
+accepted meanings, so the detail tab has alternates to show beside the primary one.
+
+## Scenes
+
+A four-button bar at the top switches scenes without a rebuild. Each scene is the same three lines —
+install the session, then let the store judge it if the scene is about a judgement — so a scene
+renders whatever *that build* does with that input.
+
+| Scene | Session | Driver action | Head renders | Baseline renders |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `meaning` | meaning prompt, open | type a wrong answer, tap the keyboard's Done, tap Done again | wrong stop, then the retry armed | same (the stop is not what changed) |
+| `reading-first` | the pair ordered by `buildWaniKaniPromptOrder([2], () => 0.1)` | none needed | **Reading** prompt | **Meaning** prompt (the baseline asks a meaning first whatever the draw) |
+| `mixed-input` | reading prompt, `sひゅう` in the field, `wkCheck` on install | none needed | entry **refused**, note shown, nothing judged or counted | entry **judged**, `Incorrect` |
+| `wrong-stop` | meaning prompt, wrong answer judged on install | tap `Show answer` | Primary meaning large, **Other meanings** small | all four meanings as one flat list |
+
+`reading-first` and `mixed-input` read the same pinned order, and the cursor lands on the reading
+prompt in both builds: the baseline's builder takes one argument and ignores the draw, so the same call
+yields the meaning-first order — which is exactly the before-state of the drawn-lead change.
+
+## Capture procedure
+
+- **Open with the test IME off** (`agent-device open … testIme: false`, the CLI's `--no-test-ime`), so
+  the real Gboard stays the selected IME; check `dumpsys input_method` for
+  `com.google.android.inputmethod.latin` before typing anything.
+- **Press the visible Done key**: target it by screenshot-derived coordinates or by its own
+  accessibility node, never `agent-device keyboard enter`/`return` — those inject a hardware
+  `KEYCODE_ENTER`, which is the very thing this harness exists to avoid.
+- **Assert the scene is active before capturing.** The scene buttons publish a session and, when the
+  step is busy, `startReviews` no-ops; a snapshot must show the scene's own screen (its pill, its note)
+  before the still is taken.
+- **`mixed-input` must still refuse `sひゅう`** on the head build after the guard moved to finished
+  kana: the latin run is not convertible, so the finished text is still `sひゅう` and is still refused.
+- Nothing is ever answered correctly, so no subject is completed.
+
+## No network, by construction
+
+The fixture's entire surface on the store is `getState`, `subscribe`, `startReviews`, `wkEntry`,
+`wkCheck`, `wkContinue`. The store's native calls, and whether the fixture can reach them:
+
+| Call | Reached from | Fixture |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `readingAnswer` | a reading judgement | reachable — a local kana fold, no I/O |
+| `submitReview` | `submitWaniKani`, the one place a review is posted | **replaced with a no-op before the session is installed** |
+| `reviewQueue` | `enterWaniKaniReview`, which `startReviews` calls only when no paused session exists | **stubbed to a resolved promise**, and the paused session is installed first |
+| `isConfigured`, `getLearningPreferences`, `lessonsQueue`, `connect`, `startLesson` | the hub, lesson and connect paths | never called |
+
+Both members the fixture overrides were checked to be functions in these two builds — `typeof
+internals.submitWaniKani === "function"` and the same for `enterWaniKaniReview` — and the install
+**fails closed** if either has moved: it publishes no session and never calls `startReviews`, so
+nothing can be asked of the network. The names are verified for these two artifacts, not guaranteed
+for a future build. If `pausedReview` were renamed instead, the store would simply not publish the
+session and the same stubbed queue read would leave a fallback card — again no request.
+
+On top of that, **the AVD these captures run on holds no WaniKani token** (the account was
+disconnected), so there is no account for the harness to reach even by accident, and no install of it
+touches app data (`-r`/`reinstall`, never a fresh install).
+
+## Build and verify
+
+```sh
+# head
+ENTRY_FILE=.evidence-fixture/index.js ./gradlew --no-daemon :app:assembleDebug -PreactNativeArchitectures=x86_64
+# baseline
+cd /tmp/gaten-dev-baseline && ENTRY_FILE=.evidence-fixture/index.js ./gradlew --no-daemon :app:assembleDebug -PreactNativeArchitectures=x86_64
+
+# types (the repo's own config does not include this directory)
+npx tsc --noEmit -p .evidence-fixture/tsconfig.json
+
+# the APK carries the fixture, not the app
+unzip -p <apk> assets/index.android.bundle > /tmp/b.bundle
+grep -ac "Fixture subject: synthetic" /tmp/b.bundle   # 1
+grep -ac "No recent searches found" /tmp/b.bundle     # 0
+```
+
+The entry override is the React Native Gradle plugin's own precedence: `ENTRY_FILE` →
+`react { entryFile }` → `index.android.js` → `index.js` (`PathUtils.kt`), resolved against
+`react { root = file("..") }`. `debuggableVariants` is already empty in `app/build.gradle.kts`, so a
+debug variant embeds its bundle and needs no Metro server. No production file changes, no init script,
+no second Gradle module, no change to any real build entry.
+
+## Limits
+
+- It reaches three private members of the store (`pausedReview`, `submitWaniKani`,
+  `enterWaniKaniReview`) and fails closed on the two it overrides, as above.
+- One subject, two prompts. It does not exercise the queue read, the hub, the lesson quiz, or the
+  lookup overlay, and it proves nothing about a real account.
+- The session object carries `entryRefused`, a field only the head build's store has. On the baseline
+  it is inert — that build's screen never reads it — which is why `mixed-input` is judged there
+  instead of refused.
+- Hermes stores a string containing non-ASCII as UTF-16, so only ASCII markers can be grepped out of
+  the bundle; the markers above are chosen for that.
+- This directory is evidence scaffolding: it must not be committed, and it is deleted once the
+  capture is reviewed.
